{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AxmXWfEFNAmEZBwcj1nv3w","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review 2025 2026 reviewer form scoring rubric\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"Main Conference - ACL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://2026.aclweb.org/calls/main_conference_papers/\"},{\"title\":\"Dates and Venues – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/dates\"},{\"title\":\"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026\"},{\"title\":\"ACLRollingReview (@ReviewAcl) / X\",\"url\":\"https://x.com/reviewacl\"},{\"title\":\"ACL ARR 2025 February | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FFebruary\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) 2025-2026 reviewer form and scoring rubric:\n\n## Scoring System\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n### Soundness Score\nThe soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review. If you give a low Soundness score without finding any major faults, this means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation, and you need to revise it.\n\n### Excitement Score\nSuch preferences are more subjective and should be reflected in a separate excitement score, which is orthogonal to the assessment of the soundness of the paper.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements\n\nAll reviewers must familiarize themselves with the latest version of the ARR reviewer guidelines and perform the reviews on time and in line with ARR requirements.\n\nThe actual detailed review form and complete scoring rubric appear to be available on the ACL Rolling Review website at aclrollingreview.org/reviewform, but the specific numerical scales and detailed rubric criteria were not fully displayed in these search results. For the most current and complete scoring rubric, I'd recommend visiting the ARR website directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2df59a54-ef24-4a14-a88b-11610600ad72","uuid":"6c1aac7b-35e9-42b9-8be1-bcf1eadf3bc8","timestamp":"2026-05-13T09:02:34.616Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review 2025 2026 reviewer form scoring rubric","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_013n1wt9qEEizsQUZ5cSRfYw","content":[{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing"},{"title":"Main Conference - ACL 2026","url":"https://2026.aclweb.org/calls/main_conference_papers/"},{"title":"Dates and Venues – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/dates"},{"title":"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026"},{"title":"ACLRollingReview (@ReviewAcl) / X","url":"https://x.com/reviewacl"},{"title":"ACL ARR 2025 February | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FFebruary"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) 2025-2026 reviewer form and scoring rubric:\n\n## Scoring System\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n### Soundness Score\nThe soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review. If you give a low Soundness score without finding any major faults, this means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation, and you need to revise it.\n\n### Excitement Score\nSuch preferences are more subjective and should be reflected in a separate excitement score, which is orthogonal to the assessment of the soundness of the paper.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements\n\nAll reviewers must familiarize themselves with the latest version of the ARR reviewer guidelines and perform the reviews on time and in line with ARR requirements.\n\nThe actual detailed review form and complete scoring rubric appear to be available on the ACL Rolling Review website at aclrollingreview.org/reviewform, but the specific numerical scales and detailed rubric criteria were not fully displayed in these search results. For the most current and complete scoring rubric, I'd recommend visiting the ARR website directly."],"durationSeconds":6.0395786860000005}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013DWKVGH4jsbQjVDPgnung9","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2026 ARR reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Call for Main Conference Papers - EMNLP 2026\",\"url\":\"https://2026.emnlp.org/calls/main_conference_papers/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"},{\"title\":\"Dates and Venues – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/dates\"},{\"title\":\"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)\",\"url\":\"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N\",\"url\":\"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Call for Main Conference Papers -\",\"url\":\"https://2026.eacl.org/calls/papers/\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"}]\n\nI found information about EMNLP 2026 and ARR reviewer guidelines. Here's what the search results show:\n\n## EMNLP 2026 ARR Process\n\nEMNLP 2026 will use ACL Rolling Review (ARR) as a reviewing system, but final decisions will be made by the conference. Submissions and commitment will be performed via the Open Review platform, with authors following a two-step process: submitting articles to ARR for reviews and meta-reviews, then committing their reviewed articles to EMNLP 2026, where Senior Area Chairs and Program Chairs make final acceptance decisions.\n\n## Review Timeline for EMNLP 2026\n\nIf reviewers receive assignments, reviews must be completed by July 6, or meta-reviews by July 29.\n\n## ARR Reviewer Guidelines\n\nAll reviewers must familiarize themselves with the latest version of the ARR reviewer guidelines and perform reviews on time and in line with ARR requirements. If reviewers become aware or can guess the authors' identity, they should disclose that in the ARR review form, which contains questions about the reviewers' knowledge of author identity.\n\nThe detailed ARR reviewer guidelines are available at: http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\n\nFor the specific review form fields and detailed submission information, you can visit the ARR Call for Papers page at: http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2df59a54-ef24-4a14-a88b-11610600ad72","uuid":"e859b5b2-9b93-4e2f-ab14-5c286d4f7909","timestamp":"2026-05-13T09:02:35.299Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2026 ARR reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01PbzhhCRJjkFY1iVtkgJZZH","content":[{"title":"Call for Main Conference Papers - EMNLP 2026","url":"https://2026.emnlp.org/calls/main_conference_papers/"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"},{"title":"Dates and Venues – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/dates"},{"title":"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)","url":"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N","url":"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026"},{"title":"Call for Main Conference Papers -","url":"https://2026.eacl.org/calls/papers/"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"}]},"I found information about EMNLP 2026 and ARR reviewer guidelines. Here's what the search results show:\n\n## EMNLP 2026 ARR Process\n\nEMNLP 2026 will use ACL Rolling Review (ARR) as a reviewing system, but final decisions will be made by the conference. Submissions and commitment will be performed via the Open Review platform, with authors following a two-step process: submitting articles to ARR for reviews and meta-reviews, then committing their reviewed articles to EMNLP 2026, where Senior Area Chairs and Program Chairs make final acceptance decisions.\n\n## Review Timeline for EMNLP 2026\n\nIf reviewers receive assignments, reviews must be completed by July 6, or meta-reviews by July 29.\n\n## ARR Reviewer Guidelines\n\nAll reviewers must familiarize themselves with the latest version of the ARR reviewer guidelines and perform reviews on time and in line with ARR requirements. If reviewers become aware or can guess the authors' identity, they should disclose that in the ARR review form, which contains questions about the reviewers' knowledge of author identity.\n\nThe detailed ARR reviewer guidelines are available at: http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\n\nFor the specific review form fields and detailed submission information, you can visit the ARR Call for Papers page at: http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"],"durationSeconds":7.242152657999999}}
