{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018XEWQPpNF6p8R3MpS1BLjs","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"site:aclrollingreview.org reviewform scoring scale soundness excitement overall\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Response to ACL 2023 Questions\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/ACL-2023-session/\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Changelog\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/changelog\"},{\"title\":\"ARR SAC Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/sacguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Submission Form Fields\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/submissionform\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) scoring scale for soundness, excitement, and overall assessment:\n\n## Soundness Score\n\nThe soundness scale includes: 5 = Excellent (one of the most thorough studies), 4 = Strong (sufficient support for all claims), and 3 = Acceptable (sufficient support for main claims). The soundness evaluation considers whether the paper is sufficiently sound and thorough, clearly states scientific claims with adequate support, and for experimental papers, evaluates the depth/breadth of research questions, technical soundness of experiments, and methodological validity.\n\n## Excitement Score\n\nThe excitement scale includes: 5 = Highly Exciting (would recommend to others and/or attend presentation), and 4 = Exciting (would mention to others and/or make effort to attend presentation). Excitement is subjective and doesn't necessarily follow field popularity; papers may be seen as transformational/innovative/surprising due to conceptual breakthroughs, evidence challenging assumptions, possible community impact, or relevance to the reviewer's own research.\n\n## Overall Recommendation Score\n\nThe overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for paper outcome if committed to an *ACL venue, reflecting soundness, excitement, and other factors like novelty and impact. Starting with February 2025, ARR reviewers provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2df59a54-ef24-4a14-a88b-11610600ad72","uuid":"f2d9666e-efd3-4ff8-aaf3-7e41feb0807d","timestamp":"2026-05-13T09:02:46.306Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"site:aclrollingreview.org reviewform scoring scale soundness excitement overall","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01KyUemCo7qENvHBGcEKT9P3","content":[{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"Response to ACL 2023 Questions","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/ACL-2023-session/"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"ARR Changelog","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/changelog"},{"title":"ARR SAC Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/sacguidelines"},{"title":"Submission Form Fields","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/submissionform"},{"title":"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing"}]},"Based on the search results, here's information about the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) scoring scale for soundness, excitement, and overall assessment:\n\n## Soundness Score\n\nThe soundness scale includes: 5 = Excellent (one of the most thorough studies), 4 = Strong (sufficient support for all claims), and 3 = Acceptable (sufficient support for main claims). The soundness evaluation considers whether the paper is sufficiently sound and thorough, clearly states scientific claims with adequate support, and for experimental papers, evaluates the depth/breadth of research questions, technical soundness of experiments, and methodological validity.\n\n## Excitement Score\n\nThe excitement scale includes: 5 = Highly Exciting (would recommend to others and/or attend presentation), and 4 = Exciting (would mention to others and/or make effort to attend presentation). Excitement is subjective and doesn't necessarily follow field popularity; papers may be seen as transformational/innovative/surprising due to conceptual breakthroughs, evidence challenging assumptions, possible community impact, or relevance to the reviewer's own research.\n\n## Overall Recommendation Score\n\nThe overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for paper outcome if committed to an *ACL venue, reflecting soundness, excitement, and other factors like novelty and impact. Starting with February 2025, ARR reviewers provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation."],"durationSeconds":6.623268763999997}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017ipZ9n6kBB6Sh6izE2kvDt","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review review form 2025 soundness score 1-5 excitement overall assessment scale\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/acguidelines.md at main · yoshitomo-matsubara/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/yoshitomo-matsubara/aclrollingreview/blob/main/acguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/acguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/acguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \\\"Publish or Perish\\\" Circus | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found detailed information about the ACL Rolling Review form for 2025. Here's what I found:\n\n## Scoring Scales for 2025\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n### Soundness Score (1-5 scale)\n\nThe soundness score uses a 1-5 scale to assess the technical quality:\n- 5 = Excellent: This study is one of the most thorough I have seen, given its type.\n- 4 = Strong: This study provides sufficient support for all of its claims. Some extra experiments could be nice, but not essential.\n- 3 = Acceptable: This study provides sufficient support for its main claims.\n\nThe soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review. If you give a low Soundness score without finding any major faults, this means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation, and you need to revise it.\n\n### Excitement Score (1-5 scale)\n\n- 5 = Highly Exciting: I would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation in a conference.\n- 4 = Exciting: I would mention this paper to others and/or make an effort to attend its presentation in a conference.\n- 1 = Not Exciting: this paper does not resonate with me, and I don't think it would with others in the *ACL community (e.g. it is in no way related to computational processing of language).\n\nExcitement scores reflect our personal taste, and so do not necessarily come with explicit reasons.\n\n### Overall Assessment Score\n\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2df59a54-ef24-4a14-a88b-11610600ad72","uuid":"e9f85f80-3538-4f21-8d02-3d57cc472033","timestamp":"2026-05-13T09:02:48.220Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review review form 2025 soundness score 1-5 excitement overall assessment scale","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_015mwf7XVgM3d9GRjHaXBoVz","content":[{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/acguidelines.md at main · yoshitomo-matsubara/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/yoshitomo-matsubara/aclrollingreview/blob/main/acguidelines.md"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/acguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/acguidelines.md"},{"title":"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \"Publish or Perish\" Circus | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus"}]},"Based on the search results, I found detailed information about the ACL Rolling Review form for 2025. Here's what I found:\n\n## Scoring Scales for 2025\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n### Soundness Score (1-5 scale)\n\nThe soundness score uses a 1-5 scale to assess the technical quality:\n- 5 = Excellent: This study is one of the most thorough I have seen, given its type.\n- 4 = Strong: This study provides sufficient support for all of its claims. Some extra experiments could be nice, but not essential.\n- 3 = Acceptable: This study provides sufficient support for its main claims.\n\nThe soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review. If you give a low Soundness score without finding any major faults, this means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation, and you need to revise it.\n\n### Excitement Score (1-5 scale)\n\n- 5 = Highly Exciting: I would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation in a conference.\n- 4 = Exciting: I would mention this paper to others and/or make an effort to attend its presentation in a conference.\n- 1 = Not Exciting: this paper does not resonate with me, and I don't think it would with others in the *ACL community (e.g. it is in no way related to computational processing of language).\n\nExcitement scores reflect our personal taste, and so do not necessarily come with explicit reasons.\n\n### Overall Assessment Score\n\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact."],"durationSeconds":8.213498625}}
